# Test: ze config history - is refused, and the message says why.
#
# VALIDATES: a stdin-only NEGATIVE assertion is reachable from a .ci. History
#   lists the rollback/ revisions stored beside a config file, and a config read
#   from standard input has none, so cmdHistory (internal/component/config/cli/
#   cmd_history.go) refuses the "-" by name before it opens a store.
# PREVENTS: the branch being unreachable. The runner replaced the "-" with a
#   path, so history ran against a real file and the refusal could not be
#   asserted from any .ci at all.
#
# Discrimination: delete the cliio.IsStdin guard in cmdHistory and this test goes
#   red, because the command then opens the substituted path and exits 0 with a
#   revision list. Exit 2 is exitError (internal/component/config/cli/main.go).
#   The exit code alone does NOT discriminate: history against a substituted
#   path also exits 2, and that arm was measured passing the exit assertion
#   while the stderr line was absent. The stderr assertion is what makes this
#   test about the stdin refusal.

stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
bgp {
	peer peer1 {
		connection {
			remote {
				ip 127.0.0.1
			}
		}
		session {
			asn {
				local 65000
				remote 65001
			}
			router-id 1.2.3.4
		}
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config history -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=2
expect=stderr:contains=history needs on-disk revision history
